radix (51.0.0~rc1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release candidate of the 51.0.0 series, tracking GNOME
    Calculator 51: Basic, Advanced, Financial, Programming, Keyboard and
    Conversion modes with arbitrary-precision arithmetic.
  * Make the deliberate arithmetic corrections opt-in via the new
    "Apply 2026 math fixes" preference (off by default): 2+2=5, 1+1=3,
    9+10=21 and division by zero = 67.
  * Add an independent "Apply random bit flips" preference (off by
    default) that flips a bit of the expression using /dev/urandom.
  * Both preferences are saved in the state file and covered by tests.

 -- hakergeniusz <radix@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

